/*
 * Flame sensor monitor for Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+
 * Sensor : Keyes KY-026 (digital output, active-low)
 * Wiring : DO  -> GPIO17 (BCM 17, physical pin 11)
 *          VCC -> 3.3 V
 *          GND -> GND
 * Library: pigpio (modern, actively maintained; not wiringPi)
 *
 * Behavior:
 *   Polls GPIO17 every 100 ms.  On a falling edge (HIGH -> LOW)
 *   the program prints "FLAME DETECTED" and appends a timestamped
 *   entry to flame_log.txt (opened in append mode, flushed immediately).
 *   Duplicate alerts are suppressed while the line remains LOW.
 *   SIGINT/SIGTERM triggers graceful shutdown: line released, chip closed,
 *   log file closed.
